                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_189">Durham. Benedictine
                        cathedral priory of St Cuthbert</orgName><p>Erased inscription on fol. 2v:
                        [ . . . . . . ] quis alienauerit al(?) [ . . . .] sit [ . . . ]'.</p><p>Fol.
                        2v: 'Liber domini Ricardi [ . . . . ]dell de empcione a domino Roberti Rok'.
                        (Richard Riddell occurs as a monk of Durham between 1485/6 and 1501; Robert
                        Rok fl. 1491–1505; Durham Cathedral A.IV.29, fol. 149v has 'Ihesus est amor
                        meus Robertus Rok', s. xv.)</p><p>Fol. 35v: 'C heghington Monachus Dunelm''.
                        (Cuthbert Heghington occurs 1520–39; the name 'Dompnus C. heghyngton' is in
                        the Durham Liber Vitae, fol. 83r.)</p><p>(Medieval binding: chain-staple
                        intact at foot of back cover.)</p><p>Various scribbles on flyleaf, 'Nomina
                        messorum . . .', etc. Also 'Compotus domini Willelmi Cuthbert' magistri de .
                        . .', and 'Recepcio pecunie quam ego recepi de tali homine manente in nouo
                        castro'. (William Cuthbert senior occurs 1453, d. 1474 or 1475; William
                        Cuthbert jnr occurs 1462/3 and until 1497.</p><p> </p></provenance>
               </history>
